      "url": "https://aquariumdrunkard.com/2026/09/22/indio-da-cuica-zing-zing/",
      "summary": "At 70, Brazilian percussionist Índio da Cuíca reinvented himself as one of the country’s strangest musical voices. His cuíca—usually a squeaky rhythmic accent—is transformed into a melodic instrument of uncanny virtuosity, set against samba, capoeira, Afro-Brazilian spirituals and warped pop forms. On Zing Zing , that “avant-traditional” vision expands further, as cavaquinho, pandeiro, berimbau and bandolim collide with guitars, synths and samples. Samba music from some parallel universe. The post Índio da Cuíca :: Zing Zing first appeared on Aquarium Drunkard .",
